      "message": "Mostly curious, did something warn about this? `auto` with destructuring like this is difficult to understand, since the `auto` here resolves to the type of the thing to be destructured (here a `std::tuple\u003cconst Uniform, const std::vector\u003cSkMeshSpecification::Uniform\u003e` with whatever attributes or ref qualifiers are added) and then the types of the identifiers (here `actual` and `expected`) are inferred from that and are always lvalue references (this change does not affect that). `SkMakeZip` will return an rvalue so either `const auto\u0026` or `auto\u0026\u0026` will work. `const auto\u0026\u0026` works but seems strange since it does not affect the constness of `actual` and `expected` (they\u0027re const either way because the tuple template types are const). It\u0027s just surprising to see a const rvalue reference (though they can be useful for method overload selection).",
